WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:04.160
Throughout its 12-season run, "The Big&nbsp;
Bang Theory" remained a ratings and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.160 --> 00:00:09.680
cultural juggernaut. But just because something is&nbsp;
popular does not automatically mean it is perfect.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.680 --> 00:00:13.280
Here are some questionable things&nbsp;
we ignore in “The Big Bang Theory”.

00:00:13.920 --> 00:00:17.680
Fans who only started watching "The&nbsp;
Big Bang Theory" after Howard married&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.680 --> 00:00:21.760
Bernadette might not realize how big of&nbsp;
a creep Howard was before settling down&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.760 --> 00:00:26.000
with the love of his life. In the earliest&nbsp;
seasons, Howard was basically a predator,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:30.560
and Penny was often the unfortunate&nbsp;
recipient of his unwanted attentions.

00:00:30.560 --> 00:00:35.760
One of the most unsettling throwaway jokes from&nbsp;
early on in the show was when Howard asked Penny&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.760 --> 00:00:40.800
if she would have opened the door if she knew&nbsp;
he was standing outside. To this, Penny replies,

00:00:40.800 --> 00:00:43.840
"Not since I found out that the teddy&nbsp;
bear you gave me had a webcam in it."

00:00:45.760 --> 00:00:50.640
This was not even the only time Howard tried&nbsp;
to use technology to spy on an attractive woman&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.640 --> 00:00:55.680
without her consent. He and Raj went to great&nbsp;
lengths to figure out the location of the house&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.680 --> 00:00:58.960
from "America's Next Top Model"&nbsp;
where all the models were staying,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.960 --> 00:01:02.480
even making illegal use of a&nbsp;
government satellite in the process.

00:01:02.480 --> 00:01:07.200
Howard's antics are always played for laughs,&nbsp;
but it is clear that his behavior rubs every&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:10.880
woman he meets the wrong way. This was&nbsp;
confirmed when he tried to kiss Penny,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.880 --> 00:01:16.240
and she punched him in the eye in retaliation. The&nbsp;
truth is, if the show was even slightly realistic,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.240 --> 00:01:20.240
a lot of the stunts Howard pulled to try to&nbsp;
get with women could have landed him in jail.

00:01:20.800 --> 00:01:23.840
"The Big Bang Theory" was a show&nbsp;
that thrived on making jokes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:23.840 --> 00:01:28.320
about stereotypes. As the show's rare&nbsp;
main character who's also non-white,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.320 --> 00:01:32.800
Raj was often the subject of mockery, based&nbsp;
on his Indian heritage. Over the years,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:32.800 --> 00:01:36.720
many jokes were made about Raj coming from&nbsp;
a country that is poor and overpopulated,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.720 --> 00:01:40.480
where animals are considered "magic," and&nbsp;
where the culture and religion were silly.

00:01:42.960 --> 00:01:44.000
“That’s very offensive.”

00:01:45.520 --> 00:01:50.080
After a time, the show eased up on the Indian&nbsp;
jokes somewhat, but the attacks against Raj&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.080 --> 00:01:54.480
became more personal. Every aspect of the&nbsp;
character's life, from his lack of a romantic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.480 --> 00:01:59.040
partner to personal interests and physical&nbsp;
appearance, were constantly made fun of. Worse,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.040 --> 00:02:03.120
it was usually Raj's best friend Howard&nbsp;
making those jokes, to the extent that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:03.120 --> 00:02:07.840
the two had a brief falling out because Raj did&nbsp;
not like the way Howard constantly bullied him.

00:02:07.840 --> 00:02:11.440
The end of the show did nothing to&nbsp;
give Raj any sort of a redemption arc.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:11.440 --> 00:02:15.760
He remained the only main character to not&nbsp;
have a special someone when the series ended,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:15.760 --> 00:02:20.400
due to facing one bitter disappointment in&nbsp;
his love life after another. He was also&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:20.400 --> 00:02:24.320
shown to have become much more dependent&nbsp;
on his parents for financial support,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.320 --> 00:02:29.280
and essentially replaced Sheldon as the&nbsp;
man-child unable to function as a mature adult.

00:02:29.920 --> 00:02:34.240
Before Jim Parsons made Sheldon the star of&nbsp;
the show, "The Big Bang Theory" was mainly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.240 --> 00:02:39.120
about Leonard trying to desperately date Penny.&nbsp;
In time, after many false stops and starts,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:39.120 --> 00:02:43.680
Leonard and Penny finally become a couple when&nbsp;
they tie the knot and move in together. But&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:43.680 --> 00:02:47.680
that was far from the happily-ever-after&nbsp;
scenario that fans had been expecting.

00:02:47.680 --> 00:02:51.200
Soon after their marriage, fans started&nbsp;
noticing that Penny was becoming more&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:51.200 --> 00:02:54.560
than a little mean towards Leonard.&nbsp;
She belittled his accomplishments,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.560 --> 00:02:59.200
made fun of his relationship with his mother,&nbsp;
and frequently made fun of him in group settings.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:59.200 --> 00:03:04.400
When Penny and Raj were discussing how Howard&nbsp;
constantly makes mean-spirited comments about Raj,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:04.400 --> 00:03:09.040
he points out that Penny does the same thing&nbsp;
with Leonard. She agrees with that assessment.

00:03:09.040 --> 00:03:13.760
But perhaps the biggest sign that all was not well&nbsp;
in Penny and Leonard's marriage, due to Penny's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:13.760 --> 00:03:18.640
attitude, occurs in the episode "The Romance&nbsp;
Recalibration." At first, Penny thinks Leonard has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:18.640 --> 00:03:23.200
stopped trying in their relationship since getting&nbsp;
married. But then Leonard points out the opposite.

00:03:23.200 --> 00:03:26.400
“I’m the one who’s made all the effort&nbsp;
in this relationship since day one,

00:03:26.400 --> 00:03:28.400
please tell me what more i could do!"

00:03:28.880 --> 00:03:32.640
Later seasons of "The Big Bang Theory" gave&nbsp;
us strong female characters and storylines,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:32.640 --> 00:03:35.920
thanks to the addition of Amy and&nbsp;
Bernadette to the main cast. But this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:35.920 --> 00:03:39.680
only serves to highlight how the early&nbsp;
seasons of the show were only interested&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:39.680 --> 00:03:44.160
in presenting women as the mysterious&nbsp;
"other," almost like they were aliens.

00:03:44.160 --> 00:03:48.480
The central premise upon which the show itself&nbsp;
was built had to do with the awkwardness&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:48.480 --> 00:03:53.520
of the main four male characters in social&nbsp;
situations, particularly pertaining to women.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:53.520 --> 00:03:58.000
Howard acts like a thirsty creep around&nbsp;
females; Raj is literally unable to even&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:58.000 --> 00:04:02.000
speak to them without getting drunk; Sheldon&nbsp;
has no interest in interacting with them;&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:02.000 --> 00:04:06.080
and Leonard, perhaps the most "normal"&nbsp;
of the group, can't even ask out Penny,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:06.080 --> 00:04:10.000
or any other attractive woman, due&nbsp;
to a crippling inferiority complex.

00:04:10.000 --> 00:04:14.320
Because of this setup, females on the show&nbsp;
were all too often presented as one-dimensional&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:14.320 --> 00:04:18.800
characters whose only contribution to the&nbsp;
plot was being hot, or whether or not the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:18.800 --> 00:04:22.720
male characters had a chance of sleeping with&nbsp;
them. This trend was summed up perfectly in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:22.720 --> 00:04:27.600
episode "The Justice League Recombination." When&nbsp;
Sheldon questions whether Penny's Wonder Woman&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:27.600 --> 00:04:32.000
outfit is authentic enough without a black wig,&nbsp;
Howard dismisses his concerns with the remark.

00:04:32.640 --> 00:04:34.560
"Relax. No one's going to be looking at her hair."

00:04:39.040 --> 00:04:43.520
In a sea of awkward, antisocial geeks, "The&nbsp;
Big Bang Theory" initially presented Penny as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:43.520 --> 00:04:48.160
the sole voice of reason. The street-smart,&nbsp;
kind-hearted simpleton did not mind being&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:48.160 --> 00:04:51.600
friends with geeks, and even helped them&nbsp;
open up to the rest of the world. This,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:51.600 --> 00:04:55.040
however, is far from the reality of&nbsp;
Penny's relationship with the guys.

00:04:55.040 --> 00:04:58.960
Penny is shown to be clearly aware of the&nbsp;
effect her looks have on Leonard, Raj,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:58.960 --> 00:05:02.480
and Howard, and she often uses it to&nbsp;
her advantage. She eats food that the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:02.480 --> 00:05:06.480
guys order without paying her share. She&nbsp;
steals their Wi-Fi and uses their brains&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:06.480 --> 00:05:10.160
whenever she needs something technical&nbsp;
done. Even worse, she made Leonard go&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:10.160 --> 00:05:14.800
to her ex-boyfriend's house to pick up her&nbsp;
things after only knowing him for a few days,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:14.800 --> 00:05:19.200
leading to Leonard getting bullied by her ex.&nbsp;
Both him and Sheldon get their pants taken.

00:05:19.840 --> 00:05:20.340
“Leonard.”

00:05:21.040 --> 00:05:21.680
“What?”

00:05:21.680 --> 00:05:23.040
“My mom bought me those pants.”

00:05:23.040 --> 00:05:23.840
“I’m sorry.”

00:05:25.680 --> 00:05:29.600
It is also shown that Penny is&nbsp;
aware of her manipulative behavior,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:29.600 --> 00:05:33.040
since she grows insecure when a new&nbsp;
pretty girl moves into their building&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:33.040 --> 00:05:36.240
and proceeds to use the guys in&nbsp;
exactly the same manner as her.

00:05:36.720 --> 00:05:40.800
"The Big Bang Theory" is often held up&nbsp;
as an example of a show that brought the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:40.800 --> 00:05:44.320
geek way of life into the cultural&nbsp;
mainstream. While it is true that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:44.320 --> 00:05:48.720
the show is chock-full of references to&nbsp;
the most obscure facets of geek culture,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:48.720 --> 00:05:51.760
how it explores those facets is&nbsp;
more than a little questionable.

00:05:51.760 --> 00:05:56.320
Oftentimes, the entire punch line of a joke is&nbsp;
that these grown men are actually interested&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:56.320 --> 00:06:01.200
in something so "geeky." Consider the following&nbsp;
actual joke from an actual episode of the show:

00:06:01.200 --> 00:06:04.880
"The fate of Doctor Who's Tardis will be&nbsp;
decided by a 'Game of Thrones'-inspired&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:04.880 --> 00:06:08.160
deathmatch on the battlefield of&nbsp;
Thundercats versus Transformers."

00:06:09.760 --> 00:06:11.760
That's it. That's the entire joke. Just a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:11.760 --> 00:06:15.200
bunch of references to various&nbsp;
sci-fi and fantasy franchises.

00:06:15.200 --> 00:06:19.040
Many times, the show doesn’t set up a&nbsp;
reference to an aspect of geek culture,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:19.040 --> 00:06:23.760
using that reference to create actual humor.&nbsp;
Instead, all too often, the entire joke is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:23.760 --> 00:06:28.080
showing how obsessed these man-children are&nbsp;
with something that’s somehow meant for kids.

00:06:28.640 --> 00:06:33.680
In the hands of a lesser actor, Sheldon would&nbsp;
have become the most insufferable character in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:33.680 --> 00:06:38.720
the history of television. It is a testament to&nbsp;
Jim Parsons' skill as an actor that he managed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:38.720 --> 00:06:43.280
to make audiences fall in love with Sheldon,&nbsp;
instead of viewing the character as the awful,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:43.280 --> 00:06:47.120
awful person he really is. From the start&nbsp;
of the show, Sheldon has proven himself,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:47.120 --> 00:06:52.960
time and again, to be petty, selfish, vindictive,&nbsp;
controlling, and callous. He constantly makes fun&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:52.960 --> 00:06:57.520
of his friends for not being as smart as him. He&nbsp;
has made several jokes at the expense of women.

00:06:57.520 --> 00:07:00.000
“Your ovaries are squirting so&nbsp;
much goofy juice into your brain,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:01.840
you don’t even know which way is up.”

00:07:03.360 --> 00:07:08.240
He even showed his assistant Alex graphic&nbsp;
images of human genitals without her consent.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:08.240 --> 00:07:11.840
Some of this behavior wound up getting&nbsp;
him sexual harassment accusations at work.

00:07:11.840 --> 00:07:16.160
Whenever Sheldon acts like a complete tool,&nbsp;
the show makes it clear that he does so out&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:16.160 --> 00:07:20.240
of ignorance rather than active malice.&nbsp;
That excuse would only work if Sheldon&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:20.240 --> 00:07:25.360
himself did not take offense when others act&nbsp;
inappropriately towards him. But in those cases,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:25.360 --> 00:07:29.920
Sheldon is always very quick to take offence.&nbsp;
Clearly, Sheldon has a working understanding&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:29.920 --> 00:07:33.520
of right and wrong, but his dismissive&nbsp;
attitude towards the entire human race,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:33.520 --> 00:07:37.920
including his closest friends and family,&nbsp;
makes him indifferent to any hurt he might&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:37.920 --> 00:07:42.400
cause to others. That is, until he is&nbsp;
specifically called out on his behavior.

00:07:42.960 --> 00:07:47.200
Over time, Leonard became one of the most&nbsp;
pathetic fictional characters ever created.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:47.200 --> 00:07:51.120
In the beginning, he was shown to allow Sheldon&nbsp;
to walk all over him in terms of their living&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:51.120 --> 00:07:55.520
arrangements. After marriage, Penny replaced&nbsp;
Sheldon as the person who constantly orders&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:55.520 --> 00:07:59.760
Leonard around. And then, to cap it all&nbsp;
off, we meet Leonard's mother Beverly.

00:07:59.760 --> 00:08:04.000
It would be hard to overstate just how much&nbsp;
emotional abuse Beverly subjected Leonard to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:04.000 --> 00:08:08.800
from a young age. She withheld affection, turned&nbsp;
a critical gaze on everything Leonard tried to do,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:08.800 --> 00:08:12.080
and acted dismissive towards his&nbsp;
achievements. To top it all off,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:12.080 --> 00:08:16.400
Leonard discovers that his mother subjected&nbsp;
him to a number of psychological experiments&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:16.400 --> 00:08:19.760
from an early age and published&nbsp;
the findings for the world to see.

00:08:20.320 --> 00:08:24.480
“Every time I’m around her, I turn into&nbsp;
this needy little eight year old boy.”

00:08:25.360 --> 00:08:30.240
All of this left deep scars on Leonard's psyche.&nbsp;
But in a case of adding insult to injury,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:30.240 --> 00:08:34.640
Beverly remains largely indifferent to Leonard's&nbsp;
feelings. She often acts as though Leonard is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:34.640 --> 00:08:39.040
being unduly emotional and that she had,&nbsp;
in fact, been a model mother. Even though&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:39.040 --> 00:08:43.680
Leonard and Beverly eventually reach some sort&nbsp;
of an understanding, the damage done to Leonard,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:43.680 --> 00:08:48.080
in terms of turning him into a human&nbsp;
doormat, will probably never be reversed.

00:08:48.800 --> 00:08:52.800
Sheldon is openly acknowledged to be a pretty&nbsp;
terrible person because there's very little&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:52.800 --> 00:08:57.440
artifice in him, and he doesn't try to hide&nbsp;
his true nature. But Sheldon has some tough&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:57.440 --> 00:09:01.200
competition in the "biggest douchebag"&nbsp;
department from none other than sweet,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:01.200 --> 00:09:05.280
tiny Bernadette, who is deceptively&nbsp;
sneaky about being a major bully.

00:09:05.280 --> 00:09:09.760
A prime example of Bernie's hidden nature&nbsp;
was seen way back when everyone thought she&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:09.760 --> 00:09:14.720
was sweetness and delight personified. Sheldon&nbsp;
is trumped by a physics problem and the rest&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:14.720 --> 00:09:18.880
of the group are suffering the consequences.&nbsp;
When they are all fed up, Bernie is the one&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:18.880 --> 00:09:22.880
to stand up to Sheldon. She talks to him&nbsp;
like he’s a child and sends him to bed.

00:09:22.880 --> 00:09:27.600
But the true extent of Bernadette's mean-spirited&nbsp;
nature was realized once her professional life&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:27.600 --> 00:09:32.960
came into focus. It comes to light that everyone&nbsp;
at her office is terrified of Bernadette,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:32.960 --> 00:09:37.360
even her boss. In fact, everyone working in the&nbsp;
same building as her collectively decides to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:37.360 --> 00:09:42.800
repurpose the handicapped washroom as Bernadette's&nbsp;
private lavatory after she keeps on using it.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:42.800 --> 00:09:47.840
This bullying aspect of Bernie's nature frequently&nbsp;
leaks into her private life in episodes to come,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:47.840 --> 00:09:52.480
so much so that even Penny grows wary&nbsp;
of accidentally making Bernadette angry.

00:09:53.040 --> 00:09:58.000
In general, it is repeatedly emphasized just how&nbsp;
smart and capable the male characters are when it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:58.000 --> 00:10:01.920
comes to their jobs — particularly Sheldon.&nbsp;
But just because they have the brains to be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:01.920 --> 00:10:06.000
good at their jobs doesn't mean they have the&nbsp;
ethics to go along with it. In fact, Leonard,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:06.000 --> 00:10:10.560
Sheldon, Raj, and Howard should be in jail for&nbsp;
some of the things they've done while on the job.

00:10:10.560 --> 00:10:15.600
For instance, there was the time when Leonard&nbsp;
almost divulged state secrets to a North Korean&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:15.600 --> 00:10:20.880
spy to make her sleep with him. Or when Leonard,&nbsp;
Raj, and Howard illegally tested an experimental&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:20.880 --> 00:10:25.920
rocket fuel formula in a public area and blew up&nbsp;
their residential building's elevator as a result.

00:10:25.920 --> 00:10:29.840
Then there's the time when Howard crashed&nbsp;
the Mars Rover space vehicle while trying&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:29.840 --> 00:10:34.160
to impress a random girl he met in a bar. And&nbsp;
let's not forget when Sheldon and Leonard tried&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:34.160 --> 00:10:38.720
to illegally procure liquid helium through a&nbsp;
shady contact. Honestly, sometimes you have to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:38.720 --> 00:10:42.720
wonder how the guys have managed to stay out&nbsp;
of jail and hold onto their jobs for so long.

